/// ROLE: context:h1
/// CONTENT: Expand Your Horizons with Artec: new {user:kind}-oriented, {user:value} and {user:matter} Modules

/// ROLE: context:p
/// CONTENT: At Artec, we're always looking to innovate and adapt to the ever-changing creative landscape. To help you kickstart a successful career, we're developing new {user:kind} modules that align with the most in-demand skills and technologies. Our modules are carefully designed to build upon each other, ensuring a seamless learning experience.


/// ROLE: context:p
/// CONTENT: Here are some ideas for our new {user:kind}-oriented modules.


/// ROLE: module: 1
/// NAME: Intro to Programming for Designers (DP)
/// TYPE: basic
/// PLACE/INDEX: 1
/// CONTENT:
/// Get a crash course in programming, specifically tailored for designers. Learn the fundamentals of coding, such as logic, variables, functions, and loops in a graphical, visually-oriented programming environment.


/// ROLE: module: 2
/// NAME: Creative Coding (CC)
/// TYPE: basic/intermediate
/// PLACE/INDEX: 2
/// CONTENT:
/// Build upon the fundamentals of programming and explore its creative applications. Learn algorithms, data structures, and other advanced programming concepts through a design lens, using open-source tools like Processing or p5.js.


/// ROLE: module: 3
/// NAME: Data Visualization (DV)
/// TYPE: intermediate
/// PLACE/INDEX: 3
/// CONTENT:
/// Learn how to visually represent data in engaging and meaningful ways. Understand various data visualization techniques and tools like D3.js, Tableau, or Adobe Illustrator.


/// ROLE: module: 4
/// NAME: Interactive Web Design (IWD)
/// TYPE: intermediate
/// PLACE/INDEX: 4
/// CONTENT:
/// Create dynamic and engaging web experiences by learning HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript. Understand user interaction design principles and learn to create captivating interactivity using frameworks like React and Angular.


/// ROLE: module: 5
/// NAME: Augmented Reality (AR)
/// TYPE: advanced
/// PLACE/INDEX: 5
/// CONTENT:
/// Dive into the world of Augmented Reality and learn how to create interactive, immersive experiences. Explore the possibilities of AR applications using tools like Unity, A-Frame, or ARCore.

